  "query_preview": "Forecast Discussion...\n\nLooking into the extended portion of the forecast, experimental \nsignal analysis has done quite well with the blocky pattern of late \nand has been highlighting the Sunday signal passage (11/22-23) quite \nwell.  Mid-late October signal charts have been showing another \nstrong signal passing through in the 11/24-26 time frame, just in \ntime for the Thanksgiving period.  This signal may result in some \nsort of east coast storm potential after the Thanksgiving holiday \nperiod.  A few more signal show up around the 28th/29th and perhaps \ninto 12/1-2.  The fast Pacific flow in this El Nino pattern will \nlikely keep a steady flow of systems rolling across the CONUS in the \nlate month period.  In terms of teleconnections, most of the model \nguidance suggests the pattern going to a -AO/-NAO/+PNA pattern.  The \nEPO pattern looked promising (negative for cold) favoring an \neventual troughing pattern across the eastern CONUS to close out \nNovember and into December.  However, the last few runs have been \nshowing the EPO dip into the negative range in the 11/21-23 period \nbut remaining rather neutral for late November into December. Should \na negative EPO develop, then the risks for a colder pattern will \ntrend higher.  Overall, looking at the last week of forecasts from \nthe extended models suggest that predictability in the overall \npattern will be quite limited, maybe to perhaps only 6-8 days of \nlead time.",
